    {
      "id": "l20q8vj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.2 Administrative Divisions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cwk0tdt",
      "content": "The state is divided into 5 divisions, 33 districts, sub-divisions, tehsils, blocks, and village panchayats. The district collector (IAS officer) heads each district and is responsible for land administration, law and order, and implementation of government schemes."
    },
    {
      "id": "y1gcq84",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.3 Panchayati Raj System"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "State Police Structure (Important for SI Exam)",
      "id": "9l1rfe8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d1c316r",
      "content": "Chhattisgarh has a three-tier Panchayati Raj system:"
    },
    {
      "id": "24q5a1t",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Gram Panchayat (Village level)",
        "Janpad Panchayat (Block level)",
        "Zila Panchayat (District level)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3dvp7qz",
      "content": "The Panchayats Extension to Scheduled Areas (PESA) Act, 1996 is implemented in the 5th Schedule areas of Chhattisgarh, giving tribal panchayats special powers over natural resources, land, and traditional customs."
    },
    {
      "id": "wi39cbe",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.4 State Police Structure (Important for SI Exam)"
    },
