    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "40l3bmw",
      "content": "The Chhattisgarh Police is headed by the Director General of Police (DGP). The state is divided into police ranges, each headed by an Inspector General of Police (IGP). Districts are headed by Superintendent of Police (SP). The hierarchy from bottom to top is: Constable → Head Constable → Assistant Sub-Inspector (ASI) → Sub-Inspector (SI) → Inspector → Deputy Superintendent of Police (DSP) → Additional Superintendent of Police (ASP) → Superintendent of Police (SP) → Senior Superintendent of Police (SSP) → Deputy Inspector General (DIG) → Inspector General (IG) → Additional Director General (ADG) → Director General of Police (DGP)."
    },
