    {
      "id": "fscvvxv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.5 Important Constitutional Provisions for Chhattisgarh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s6d98g9",
      "content": "Fifth Schedule of the Constitution covers the administration of Scheduled Areas in Chhattisgarh. The Tribes Advisory Council (TAC) is constituted under the Fifth Schedule to advise the Governor on matters concerning tribal welfare. Large parts of Chhattisgarh (especially Bastar division and parts of Surguja division) fall under the Fifth Schedule Area."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Hierarchy of State Police Forces and specialized units are key topics for the Sub-Inspector (SI) Exam.",
        "Constitutional articles related to the powers of the Governor and Chief Minister in Chhattisgarh are frequently asked in CGPSC.",
        "The 3-tier Panchayati Raj hierarchy and division-wise district allocations are high-yield areas for state competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "79cjug3"
    },
